# Line endings.
#
# The repo accumulated ~150 files showing as fully modified with no content
# change, because checkouts on different machines disagreed about CRLF. That
# noise buries real diffs: one nine-line change arrived as 1,324 changed lines.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises everything to LF in the object store while
# leaving working copies alone, which is what Git wants and what every tool in
# this project (Dart, Python, Gradle) is happy with.
#
# The existing churn is NOT fixed by adding this file. Someone has to run, once,
# on a clean tree:
#
#     git add --renormalize .
#     git commit -m "chore: normalise line endings"
#
# Do that in its own commit, with nothing else in flight - it touches almost
# every file in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.wav binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.glb binary
